  "agent": {
    "note": "c004 — all 4 of your notes. (1) BG-FIRST: the baked scatter reveal plays alone (~first 22%), THEN backdrops + header + footer + KPI cards fade in (like the title beat; verified — early frame = scatter only). (2-4) BACKDROP CARDS behind the header cluster, behind the WHOLE KPI grid (gutters no longer leak scatter), and behind the WEEK footer — all theme.card (#161b22), rounded, fading in with the chrome.",
    "question": "Reads cleaner now? Open Qs: (a) the grid backdrop is the same color as the cards so the grid reads as one panel — want the backdrop a touch DARKER (#0d1117) so individual cards separate, or keep the unified panel? (b) glyph treatment still dark-cut-on-green — want white glyphs instead?",
    "response": {
      "body": "the kpi overview card and main kpi area are slightly misaligned. as is the week text. Also, the KPI Overview should fade in BEFORE the kpi charts themselves do. Finally, the KPI charts should fade in one after another. Quicker animation speed, and the next one starts right as the previous ended. So it reads as one flow.\n\nIn the square version, I still want the KPI cards to be squareish, we need to relayout.\n\nA slight relayout to all three as well. I want the FFMPEG logo to be in line with KPI OVERVIEW. Beat 1 sits floating on top left of the entire card.",
      "from": "human",
      "at": "2026-06-23T23:41:04.436Z",
      "src": "<sandbox>/sessions/2026-06-23-ffmpeg-pulse-kpi-overview/candidate-004-1080x1920.mp4",
      "images": [
